{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/client/src/client/responseCache.ts | sed -n '50,110p;480,690p'; nl -ba packages/client/src/client/client.ts | sed -n '1635,1720p'; nl -ba packages/client/test/client/responseCacheCodec.test.ts | sed -n '1,130p'; git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"    50\t    readonly params?: string;\n    51\t    readonly partition?: string;\n    52\t}\n    53\t\n    54\t/**\n    55\t * One cached response body. `value` is the JSON-serialized result document —\n    56\t * a store is a dumb string carrier and persists it verbatim; the cache owns\n    57\t * both codec halves. `stamp` is the store-generated monotonically increasing\n    58\t * write counter — opaque to callers. Derived views (e.g. a `name → Tool`\n    59\t * index) memoize against it and re-derive only when it changes. `expiresAt`\n    60\t * (absolute ms epoch, `now + ttlMs`) and `scope` are the client-computed\n    61\t * freshness metadata; the store MUST persist them and hand them back on `get`\n    62\t * so the read path can decide freshness and gate the shared-partition\n    63\t * fallback on `scope === 'public'`.\n    64\t */\n    65\texport interface CacheEntry {\n    66\t    readonly value: string;\n    67\t    readonly stamp: number;\n    68\t    readonly expiresAt?: number;\n    69\t    readonly scope?: CacheScope;\n    70\t}\n    71\t\n    72\t/**\n    73\t * The pluggable response-cache store. The interface is intentionally narrow;\n    74\t * the in-memory default is the only implementation the SDK ships.\n    75\t *\n    76\t * Every method is async-ready ({@linkcode MaybePromise}) so a Redis-style\n    77\t * store can implement the same interface without a later breaking change; the\n    78\t * in-memory default stays synchronous (plain values are valid under\n    79\t * `MaybePromise`). The `Client` `await`s every call site.\n    80\t *\n    81\t * Entries are keyed by `{method, params, partition}` where `partition` is the\n    82\t * `Client`-derived `[serverIdentity, principal]` JSON pair, so one store\n    83\t * instance is safe to share across `Client` instances connected to different\n    84\t * servers and/or principals: writes from distinct connections never collide,\n    85\t * the shared-partition read fallback is gated on the stored\n    86\t * `scope === 'public'`, and `list_changed` / `HEADER_MISMATCH` evictions are\n    87\t * scoped to the connected server's two partitions — co-tenants on a shared\n    88\t * store are unaffected. The `Client` constructor still allocates a fresh\n    89\t * {@linkcode InMemoryResponseCacheStore} per instance by default; supply your\n    90\t * own to share or persist.\n    91\t */\n    92\texport interface ResponseCacheStore {\n    93\t    get(key: CacheKey): MaybePromise<CacheEntry | undefined>;\n    94\t    /**\n    95\t     * Writes `entry` under `key` and returns the store-generated stamp the\n    96\t     * resulting {@linkcode CacheEntry} carries. The store owns the stamp\n    97\t     * counter; callers do not supply one. The caller owns `expiresAt` and\n    98\t     * `scope` (the client-computed freshness metadata); the store MUST persist\n    99\t     * them and hand them back on `get`.\n   100\t     */\n   101\t    set(key: CacheKey, entry: { value: string; expiresAt?: number; scope?: CacheScope }): MaybePromise<number>;\n   102\t    /**\n   103\t     * Drop the single entry under `key` (no-op if absent). Called for both\n   104\t     * `notifications/resources/updated` (per-URI) and the `list_changed`\n   105\t     * notifications (the list singletons live at `{method, params: '', partition}`).\n   106\t     */\n   107\t    delete(key: CacheKey): MaybePromise<void>;\n   108\t    /**\n   109\t     * Drop every entry for `method` across every partition. The `Client` does\n   110\t     * NOT call this (its `list_changed` path issues two partition-scoped\n   480\t    /**\n   481\t     * Write `value` under `{method}` unless the per-method generation moved\n   482\t     * since `capturedGen` was taken — a `list_changed` that landed mid-walk has\n   483\t     * already invalidated the result the caller is about to write, and\n   484\t     * overwriting the eviction with the stale aggregate would lose the\n   485\t     * invalidation.\n   486\t     *\n   487\t     * The value is stored as its JSON-serialized document; serialization\n   488\t     * doubles as the mutation barrier, so a caller mutating the returned\n   489\t     * aggregate cannot reach the cache or its derived indices. A value without\n   490\t     * a JSON representation fails the write into the `reportError` sink. A\n   491\t     * custom store whose `set()` throws or rejects is routed to the same sink\n   492\t     * and the write resolves.\n   493\t     *\n   494\t     * `freshness` carries the client-computed `expiresAt` (absolute ms epoch,\n   495\t     * `now + ttlMs`) and the server-reported `cacheScope`. The storage\n   496\t     * `partition` is derived from the scope via `_partitionFor`:\n   497\t     * `'public'` → `[serverIdentity, '']` (shared within this server);\n   498\t     * `'private'` → `[serverIdentity, cachePartition]` (so a shared store\n   499\t     * never serves a private entry to another identity). Absent `freshness`\n   500\t     * preserves the substrate write (no `expiresAt`, private partition) — the\n   501\t     * `tools/list` retain-for-schema posture: never served by\n   502\t     * {@linkcode read}'s freshness gate, always readable by\n   503\t     * {@linkcode toolDefinition}.\n   504\t     *\n   505\t     * After storing under the derived partition, the same `{method, params}`\n   506\t     * is deleted from the OPPOSITE partition (mirroring {@linkcode evictKey}'s\n   507\t     * two-partition posture). A server that flips a result's `cacheScope` for\n   508\t     * the same key would otherwise leave the previous entry in the other slot\n   509\t     * — and since `_probe` checks own-partition first, a stale private entry\n   510\t     * would shadow the fresh public one (or a stale public entry would keep\n   511\t     * serving co-tenants). Both store calls are independently guarded so a\n   512\t     * custom store's failure on one does not skip the other.\n   513\t     */\n   514\t    async write(\n   515\t        method: string,\n   516\t        value: unknown,\n   517\t        capturedGen: number,\n   518\t        freshness?: { expiresAt: number; scope: CacheScope; params?: string }\n   519\t    ): Promise<void> {\n   520\t        if ((this._evictionGeneration.get(genKey(method, freshness?.params)) ?? 0) !== capturedGen) return;\n   521\t        const params = freshness?.params ?? '';\n   522\t        const ownPartition = this._partitionFor('private');\n   523\t        const sharedPartition = this._partitionFor('public');\n   524\t        const partition = (freshness?.scope ?? 'private') === 'public' ? sharedPartition : ownPartition;\n   525\t        try {\n   526\t            await this._store.set(\n   527\t                { method, params, partition },\n   528\t                { value: encodeCacheValue(value), expiresAt: freshness?.expiresAt, scope: freshness?.scope }\n   529\t            );\n   530\t        } catch (error) {\n   531\t            this._reportError(error);\n   532\t        }\n   533\t        if (sharedPartition !== ownPartition) {\n   534\t            try {\n   535\t                await this._store.delete({\n   536\t                    method,\n   537\t                    params,\n   538\t                    partition: partition === ownPartition ? sharedPartition : ownPartition\n   539\t                });\n   540\t            } catch (error) {\n   541\t                this._reportError(error);\n   542\t            }\n   543\t        }\n   544\t    }\n   545\t\n   546\t    /**\n   547\t     * Serve the fresh cached result for `{method, params}`, or `undefined`.\n   548\t     * Freshness is checked before decoding. Every hit is freshly parsed, so\n   549\t     * the caller owns the returned value. Corrupt external-store documents\n   550\t     * are reported, deleted, and treated as misses.\n   551\t     */\n   552\t    async read(method: string, params?: string): Promise<{ value: unknown } | undefined> {\n   553\t        const entry = await this._probe(method, params);\n   554\t        if (entry?.expiresAt === undefined || !(entry.expiresAt > this.now())) return undefined;\n   555\t        try {\n   556\t            const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(entry.value);\n   557\t            if (typeof parsed !== 'object' || parsed === null || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n   558\t                throw new TypeError('cached document is not an object');\n   559\t            }\n   560\t            return { value: parsed };\n   561\t        } catch (error) {\n   562\t            this._reportError(error);\n   563\t            await this._deleteBoth(method, params ?? '');\n   564\t            return undefined;\n   565\t        }\n   566\t    }\n   567\t\n   568\t    /**\n   569\t     * Connection reset. The per-instance default store IS cleared\n   570\t     * (connection-scoped); a user-supplied store is NOT — that would defeat\n   571\t     * the only reason to supply one. The generation map and every derived\n   572\t     * index are dropped regardless: they are connection-scoped even when the\n   573\t     * backing store survives, so the next read re-derives from whatever the\n   574\t     * store still holds. The server identity returns to the pre-connect\n   575\t     * sentinel. The default impl is synchronous, so the `MaybePromise<void>`\n   576\t     * return is a plain void here and the caller need not await.\n   577\t     */\n   578\t    resetForReconnect(): void {\n   579\t        if (!this._isUserSupplied) void this._store.clear();\n   580\t        this._evictionGeneration.clear();\n   581\t        this._toolIndex = undefined;\n   582\t        this._toolOutputValidatorIndex = undefined;\n   583\t        this._serverIdentity = '';\n   584\t    }\n   585\t\n   586\t    /**\n   587\t     * The descriptor for tool `name` taken from the cached `tools/list` entry.\n   588\t     * The `name → Tool` index is memoized against the entry's `stamp` and\n   589\t     * re-derived only when the backing entry changes (mcp.d's `cachedTool`).\n   590\t     * Returns `undefined` only when no `tools/list` response is held at all,\n   591\t     * or the held list does not contain `name`.\n   592\t     *\n   593\t     * Consumed by `callTool()`'s SEP-2243 `_resolveXMcpHeaderScan` (mirroring)\n   594\t     * and, via {@linkcode outputValidator}, its output-schema validation.\n   595\t     */\n   596\t    async toolDefinition(name: string): Promise<Tool | undefined> {\n   597\t        const entry = await this._probe('tools/list');\n   598\t        if (entry === undefined) {\n   599\t            this._toolIndex = undefined;\n   600\t            return undefined;\n   601\t        }\n   602\t        if (this._toolIndex?.stamp !== entry.stamp) {\n   603\t            const list = this._decodeListTools(entry);\n   604\t            const byName = new Map<string, Tool>();\n   605\t            if (list !== undefined) for (const tool of list.tools) byName.set(tool.name, tool);\n   606\t            this._toolIndex = { stamp: entry.stamp, byName };\n   607\t        }\n   608\t        return this._toolIndex.byName.get(name);\n   609\t    }\n   610\t\n   611\t    /**\n   612\t     * The compiled output-schema validator for tool `name`, derived from the\n   613\t     * cached `tools/list` entry — same source and same stamp-keyed\n   614\t     * memoization as {@linkcode toolDefinition}. The `name → validator` index\n   615\t     * re-derives only when the backing entry's stamp changes (a refetched\n   616\t     * `tools/list` recompiles; a `list_changed` eviction drops it). Returns\n   617\t     * `undefined` when no `tools/list` is held, the tool is absent, or it has\n   618\t     * no `outputSchema`.\n   619\t     *\n   620\t     * `compile` is the caller-supplied validator-compile callback (the\n   621\t     * `Client` passes its `_jsonSchemaValidator` wrapper) so this\n   622\t     * class carries no validator-provider dependency. One tool's uncompilable\n   623\t     * `outputSchema` (e.g. an invalid `pattern` regex or unresolvable `$ref`)\n   624\t     * must not poison every other tool's `callTool` — the callback isolates\n   625\t     * that compile error per tool by returning a per-tool error variant which\n   626\t     * the index stores alongside the good ones, and `callTool` surfaces it as\n   627\t     * a typed `InvalidParams` only for that name. Because the error is held on\n   628\t     * this stamp-keyed substrate (not a parallel map), it inherits the\n   629\t     * substrate's invalidation lifecycle: a `list_changed` eviction drops it,\n   630\t     * a refetched `tools/list` re-derives it, and `resetForReconnect` clears\n   631\t     * the lot.\n   632\t     */\n   633\t    async outputValidator<V>(name: string, compile: (tool: Tool) => V | undefined): Promise<V | undefined> {\n   634\t        const entry = await this._probe('tools/list');\n   635\t        if (entry === undefined) {\n   636\t            this._toolOutputValidatorIndex = undefined;\n   637\t            return undefined;\n   638\t        }\n   639\t        if (this._toolOutputValidatorIndex?.stamp !== entry.stamp) {\n   640\t            const list = this._decodeListTools(entry) ?? { tools: [] };\n   641\t            const byName = new Map<string, unknown>();\n   642\t            for (const tool of list.tools) {\n   643\t                const compiled = compile(tool);\n   644\t                if (compiled !== undefined) byName.set(tool.name, compiled);\n   645\t            }\n   646\t            this._toolOutputValidatorIndex = { stamp: entry.stamp, byName };\n   647\t        }\n   648\t        return this._toolOutputValidatorIndex.byName.get(name) as V | undefined;\n   649\t    }\n   650\t\n   651\t    /** Decode and minimally validate the document used by derived tool views. */\n   652\t    private _decodeListTools(entry: CacheEntry): ListToolsResult | undefined {\n   653\t        try {\n   654\t            const parsed = JSON.parse(entry.value) as ListToolsResult | null;\n   655\t            if (!Array.isArray(parsed?.tools) || !parsed.tools.every(tool => tool !== null && typeof tool === 'object')) {\n   656\t                throw new TypeError('cached tools/list document has a malformed tools array');\n   657\t            }\n   658\t            return parsed;\n   659\t        } catch (error) {\n   660\t            this._reportError(error);\n   661\t            return undefined;\n   662\t        }\n   663\t    }\n   664\t}\n   665\t\n   666\t/**\n   667\t * Serialize a result document for storage. JSON.stringify throws for cycles\n   668\t * and BigInt but returns `undefined` for some top-level values; normalize both\n   669\t * cases to a descriptive TypeError.\n   670\t */\n   671\tfunction encodeCacheValue(value: unknown): string {\n   672\t    let json: string | undefined;\n   673\t    try {\n   674\t        json = JSON.stringify(value);\n   675\t    } catch (error) {\n   676\t        throw new TypeError(`cache value is not JSON-serializable: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n   677\t    }\n   678\t    if (typeof json !== 'string') throw new TypeError('cache value is not JSON-serializable: it has no JSON representation');\n   679\t    return json;\n   680\t}\n  1635\t                    `${method}: exceeded listMaxPages (${this._listMaxPages}); server pagination did not terminate`,\n  1636\t                    { method, listMaxPages: this._listMaxPages }\n  1637\t                );\n  1638\t            }\n  1639\t            seen.add(cursor);\n  1640\t            const page = (await this.request({ method, params: { ...baseParams, cursor } }, options)) as R;\n  1641\t            append(acc, page);\n  1642\t            cursor = page.nextCursor;\n  1643\t            pages++;\n  1644\t        }\n  1645\t        // Delete rather than assign `undefined`: JSON serialization drops\n  1646\t        // explicit undefined properties, so absence keeps wire and cache-hit\n  1647\t        // results observably identical.\n  1648\t        delete acc.nextCursor;\n  1649\t        finalize?.(acc);\n  1650\t        if (bypass) return acc;\n  1651\t        // The aggregate is ALWAYS written: even when the resolved TTL is ≤0\n  1652\t        // the entry is stored already-stale (mcp.d's `retainForSchema`\n  1653\t        // posture) so the `tools/list`-derived index keeps working regardless,\n  1654\t        // while the freshness gate in `_serveFromCache` never serves it.\n  1655\t        // Page-1 carries the result-level `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` (`acc` IS the\n  1656\t        // mutated page-1 object).\n  1657\t        await this._cache.write(method, acc, generation, this._freshness(acc));\n  1658\t        return acc;\n  1659\t    }\n  1660\t\n  1661\t    /**\n  1662\t     * Compute the {@linkcode ClientResponseCache.write} freshness payload from\n  1663\t     * a cacheable result body. The single seam through which the client reads\n  1664\t     * `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` (mcp.d's `cachedFetch` engine). The fields pass\n  1665\t     * through the loose result schema, so they are read off the runtime body;\n  1666\t     * a missing `ttlMs` falls back to\n  1667\t     * {@linkcode ClientOptions | ClientOptions.defaultCacheTtlMs}; an explicit server-sent\n  1668\t     * `ttlMs` (including `0` — the spec's \"immediately stale\") is honoured\n  1669\t     * as-is. The default of `0` means `expiresAt === now()` ⇒ never served,\n  1670\t     * only stored. A missing `cacheScope` is treated as `'private'` — the\n  1671\t     * spec's `'public'` grant (\"any client … MAY serve to any user\") is too\n  1672\t     * strong to infer by default, and matches this SDK's server-side stamp\n  1673\t     * default.\n  1674\t     */\n  1675\t    private _freshness(result: unknown, params?: string): { expiresAt: number; scope: CacheScope; params?: string } {\n  1676\t        const body = result as { ttlMs?: unknown; cacheScope?: unknown };\n  1677\t        const ttlMs = typeof body.ttlMs === 'number' ? body.ttlMs : this._defaultCacheTtlMs;\n  1678\t        const scope: CacheScope = body.cacheScope === 'public' ? 'public' : 'private';\n  1679\t        // Clamp at 24h (`MAX_CACHE_TTL_MS`) so a server cannot pin an entry\n  1680\t        // indefinitely; floor at 0 so a negative `ttlMs` is treated as\n  1681\t        // immediately stale (the spec's absent-or-≤0 rule).\n  1682\t        return { expiresAt: this._cache.now() + Math.min(Math.max(0, ttlMs), MAX_CACHE_TTL_MS), scope, params };\n  1683\t    }\n  1684\t\n  1685\t    /**\n  1686\t     * The cache-serving front of every cacheable verb (mcp.d's `cachedFetch`\n  1687\t     * read half): under `cacheMode: 'use'` (the default), a fresh held entry\n  1688\t     * is served and the round trip is skipped. `'refresh'` and `'bypass'`\n  1689\t     * always fetch (the caller decides whether to write). Freshness and\n  1690\t     * decoding live in {@linkcode ClientResponseCache.read}; every hit is\n  1691\t     * freshly parsed, so the caller owns it outright. A custom store whose\n  1692\t     * `get()` rejects is routed to `onerror` and treated as a miss.\n  1693\t     */\n  1694\t    private async _serveFromCache<R>(\n  1695\t        method: string,\n  1696\t        params: string | undefined,\n  1697\t        options: CacheableRequestOptions | undefined\n  1698\t    ): Promise<R | undefined> {\n  1699\t        if (options?.cacheMode === 'bypass' || options?.cacheMode === 'refresh') return undefined;\n  1700\t        const hit = await this._cache.read(method, params).catch(error => void this._reportStoreError(error));\n  1701\t        if (hit !== undefined) {\n  1702\t            // A pre-aborted caller signal must reject the same way it would on\n  1703\t            // the wire path (`Protocol.request()` wraps an already-aborted\n  1704\t            // signal as `SdkError(RequestTimeout, reason)`); without this guard\n  1705\t            // a cache hit would resolve successfully and silently swallow the\n  1706\t            // abort.\n  1707\t            if (options?.signal?.aborted) {\n  1708\t                const reason = options.signal.reason;\n  1709\t                throw reason instanceof SdkError ? reason : new SdkError(SdkErrorCode.RequestTimeout, String(reason));\n  1710\t            }\n  1711\t            return hit.value as R;\n  1712\t        }\n  1713\t        return undefined;\n  1714\t    }\n  1715\t\n  1716\t    /** Route a custom-store failure to `onerror` without aborting the surrounding dispatch. */\n  1717\t    private _reportStoreError(e: unknown): void {\n  1718\t        this.onerror?.(e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e)));\n  1719\t    }\n  1720\t\n     1\timport type { CacheEntry, CacheKey, ResponseCacheStore } from '../../src/client/responseCache';\n     2\timport { ClientResponseCache, InMemoryResponseCacheStore } from '../../src/client/responseCache';\n     3\timport { afterEach, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n     4\t\n     5\tconst savedStructuredClone = globalThis.structuredClone;\n     6\t\n     7\tafterEach(() => {\n     8\t    globalThis.structuredClone = savedStructuredClone;\n     9\t});\n    10\t\n    11\tdescribe('response cache document codec', () => {\n    12\t    it('round-trips through a serialized document without structuredClone', async () => {\n    13\t        // @ts-expect-error Simulate runtimes where the global is unavailable.\n    14\t        delete globalThis.structuredClone;\n    15\t        const store = new InMemoryResponseCacheStore();\n    16\t        const cache = new ClientResponseCache(store, true);\n    17\t        const source = { tools: [{ name: 'echo', inputSchema: { type: 'object' } }] };\n    18\t\n    19\t        await cache.write('tools/list', source, cache.captureGeneration('tools/list'), {\n    20\t            expiresAt: Date.now() + 60_000,\n    21\t            scope: 'private'\n    22\t        });\n    23\t        source.tools.length = 0;\n    24\t\n    25\t        const document = store.get({ method: 'tools/list', partition: JSON.stringify(['', '']) })?.value;\n    26\t        expect(typeof document).toBe('string');\n    27\t        expect(JSON.parse(document!).tools[0].name).toBe('echo');\n    28\t        expect(((await cache.read('tools/list'))?.value as { tools: { name: string }[] }).tools[0]?.name).toBe('echo');\n    29\t    });\n    30\t\n    31\t    it('returns a fresh caller-owned object on every cache hit', async () => {\n    32\t        const store = new InMemoryResponseCacheStore();\n    33\t        const cache = new ClientResponseCache(store, true);\n    34\t        await cache.write(\n    35\t            'tools/list',\n    36\t            { tools: [{ name: 'a', inputSchema: { type: 'object' } }] },\n    37\t            cache.captureGeneration('tools/list'),\n    38\t            { expiresAt: Date.now() + 60_000, scope: 'private' }\n    39\t        );\n    40\t\n    41\t        const first = (await cache.read('tools/list'))!.value as { tools: unknown[] };\n    42\t        first.tools.length = 0;\n    43\t        const second = (await cache.read('tools/list'))!.value as { tools: unknown[] };\n    44\t        expect(second.tools).toHaveLength(1);\n    45\t        expect(second).not.toBe(first);\n    46\t    });\n    47\t\n    48\t    it('reports non-serializable writes and leaves the slot empty', async () => {\n    49\t        const reported: unknown[] = [];\n    50\t        const store = new InMemoryResponseCacheStore();\n    51\t        const cache = new ClientResponseCache(store, true, error => reported.push(error));\n    52\t        const cyclic: { tools: unknown[]; self?: unknown } = { tools: [] };\n    53\t        cyclic.self = cyclic;\n    54\t\n    55\t        await cache.write('tools/list', cyclic, cache.captureGeneration('tools/list'), {\n    56\t            expiresAt: Date.now() + 60_000,\n    57\t            scope: 'private'\n    58\t        });\n    59\t\n    60\t        expect(reported).toHaveLength(1);\n    61\t        expect(String(reported[0])).toMatch(/not JSON-serializable/);\n    62\t        expect(await cache.read('tools/list')).toBeUndefined();\n    63\t    });\n    64\t\n    65\t    it('reports and drops a fresh corrupt external-store document', async () => {\n    66\t        const reported: unknown[] = [];\n    67\t        const deleted: CacheKey[] = [];\n    68\t        let entry: CacheEntry | undefined = {\n    69\t            value: '{ not json',\n    70\t            stamp: 1,\n    71\t            expiresAt: Date.now() + 60_000,\n    72\t            scope: 'private'\n    73\t        };\n    74\t        const store: ResponseCacheStore = {\n    75\t            get: () => entry,\n    76\t            set: () => 1,\n    77\t            delete: key => {\n    78\t                deleted.push(key);\n    79\t                entry = undefined;\n    80\t            },\n    81\t            evict: () => {},\n    82\t            clear: () => {}\n    83\t        };\n    84\t        const cache = new ClientResponseCache(store, true, error => reported.push(error));\n    85\t\n    86\t        expect(await cache.read('resources/read', 'file:///a')).toBeUndefined();\n    87\t        expect(reported).toHaveLength(1);\n    88\t        expect(deleted[0]).toMatchObject({ method: 'resources/read', params: 'file:///a' });\n    89\t        expect(await cache.read('resources/read', 'file:///a')).toBeUndefined();\n    90\t        expect(reported).toHaveLength(1);\n    91\t    });\n    92\t});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Tamamlandı.\n\n- Cache artık runtime nesneleri yerine JSON-serialize edilmiş protocol document string’leri saklıyor.\n- Cache hit’lerde document yeniden parse edilerek mutation izolasyonu korunuyor.\n- `structuredClone` bağımlılığı tamamen kaldırıldı.\n- Bozuk veya serialize edilemeyen girdiler raporlanıyor; bozuk kayıtlar silinerek cache miss’e dönüştürülüyor.\n- Parametre aynalama, tool schema index’i, TTL/scope ve cache-hit davranışı korundu.\n- Custom store sözleşmesi ve dokümantasyon `value: string` için güncellendi.\n\nDoğrulama:\n\n- Cache codec, response cache ve parametre aynalama: **70 test geçti**\n- Typecheck: geçti\n- Lint/Prettier: geçti\n- `git diff --check`: geçti\n\nTam test paketi sandbox’ın localhost dinlemeyi engellemesi nedeniyle cache dışındaki `tokenProvider` testlerinde `listen EPERM 127.0.0.1` ile bloklandı; ilgili test tek başına da aynı ortam hatasını veriyor.\n\nAna değişiklikler: [responseCache.ts](/private/tmp/capsule-baseline-worktrees/T09-codex/packages/client/src/client/responseCache.ts:54), [client.ts](/private/tmp/capsule-baseline-worktrees/T09-codex/packages/client/src/client/client.ts:1645), [responseCacheCodec.test.ts](/private/tmp/capsule-baseline-worktrees/T09-codex/packages/client/test/client/responseCacheCodec.test.ts:1)."}}
